  We do actually have a word/words in English that translates as "fu'inai":
Oof! Grrrr!, etc...

  But back to pemcrxaiku

  I had previously done two lojban haiku (although never before translated
into English):

lo xekri boxfo
co vofli cu murta fe
lo manku tsani

(The flying black sheet
 Is a curtain obscuring
 The darkened heavens.)

(composed when I saw huge numbers of crows flying overhead)

 And

lo ko selsne cu
cripu fi lo prulamdei
ro lo bavlamdei

(Become the dreamer
Of spans between yesterday
And all tomorrows)

  But, since is a new project, I will not shirk from writing a new one.

le'e po'onai
labnypre cu se catra
lei rijno danti

(Not only werewolves
 Have their existence ended
 By silver bullets.)

               --gejyspa

